"Every menu action has a clear, IMMEDIATE effect on the state the menu shows: menus configure core state (default loadout, stance loadouts, worn gear) through reducers that apply instantly, and the UI reflects the new state at once. Any DELAYED in-fiction consequence (an equip action paying a round, a future combat re-arm cost) is secondary and is the SERVER's decision to queue - the client only ever knows it is configuring the default or a stance. Never make a menu toggle wait on an act to resolve before its own state reads true."